      "## Official domain distribution",
      "## Domain 1: Professional Practice and Ethics",
      "This domain extends beyond memorizing an ethical code. It includes explaining roles, policies, fees, risks and benefits, informed consent, confidentiality, electronic communication, accommodations, documentation, referral, advocacy, supervision, consultation, competence, and self-care. The current outline also places understanding statistical concepts and research methods within this professional-practice domain.",
      "**Common mistake:** Studying ethics only as a list of prohibitions. The domain also tests proactive professional responsibilities, communication with clients, documentation, and appropriate consultation.",
      "## Domain 2: Intake, Assessment, and Diagnosis",
      "This domain covers the process of gathering, interpreting, and using client information. It includes biopsychosocial, diagnostic, cultural-formulation, and initial interviews; MSE; diagnosis and co-occurring conditions; service screening; assessment instruments; trauma and substance-use assessment; risk assessment; and evaluation of counseling effectiveness.",
      "**Common mistake:** Reducing this domain to DSM memorization. Diagnosis is included, but so are interviewing, assessment selection, risk, level of care, and outcome measurement.",
      "## Domain 3: Areas of Clinical Focus",
      "This is the broadest list of client concerns in the current outline. It includes anxiety, depression, grief, trauma, substance use, sleep, eating behavior, developmental concerns, relationships, family violence, career issues, cultural adjustment, discrimination, identity development, caregiving, aging, attachment, emotional dysregulation, and other concerns.",
      "**Common mistake:** Treating every listed concern as a request for diagnosis. Questions may instead ask about developmental context, counseling response, assessment priority, theory application, risk, or referral.",
      "## Domain 4: Treatment Planning",
      "This domain focuses on converting assessment and client priorities into a collaborative course of care. It includes short- and long-term goals, strengths and barriers, referrals, levels of care, use of assessment results, progress review, coordination with providers and supports, discharge, maintenance, and termination.",
      "**Common mistake:** Selecting a sophisticated intervention before clarifying the goal, risk, readiness, or level of care.",
      "## Domain 5: Counseling Skills and Interventions",
      "This is the largest current domain. It includes alliance, theory-based interventions, developmental and cultural alignment, individual/couple/family/group modalities, motivation, crisis intervention, safety planning, psychoeducation, communication skills, group leadership techniques, family patterns, and foundational counselor responses.",
      "**Common mistake:** Memorizing the name of a theory without knowing the counselor’s goal, role, techniques, and language within that theory.",
      "## Domain 6: Core Counseling Attributes",
      "This domain addresses the interpersonal qualities and foundational behaviors of effective counselors: self-awareness, genuineness, congruence, sensitivity to gender and multicultural issues, conflict tolerance, empathy, nonjudgment, positive regard, respect for diversity, and listening/attending/reflection.",
