      "Includes research designs, sampling, variables, hypotheses, statistics, validity threats, research ethics, needs assessment, program evaluation, evidence quality, and interpretation of findings.",
      "## Why the library teaches through these areas",
      "Knowledge is easier to build when related concepts are learned together. For example:",
      "- Erikson is best learned within a lifespan-development structure.\n- Holland and Super are best compared within career development.\n- Reliability and validity are best taught together within assessment.\n- Yalom’s therapeutic factors are best understood within group process.",
